{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BarGradedCollapse","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualSES","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.legacyOfPaged","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.legacyOfPaged","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L233-L243","doc":"**The honest discharge.** A real `PagedSS` collapsing at `E_2` supplies\n`GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2` — the hypothesis downstream theorems take.\n\nCompare `canonicalTrivial`, which supplies the same class from `PUnit`.\nBoth are `def`s and neither is an instance, so a reader of a downstream\ntheorem can see which was used; the point of this one is that there is now\nsomething to see. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.toLegacy_collapsesAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.toLegacy_collapsesAt","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L225-L231","doc":"Collapse transfers to the legacy predicate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.toLegacy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.toLegacy","kind":"def","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L213-L223","doc":"A `PagedSS` presented in the old `SpectralSequence` shape.\n\nThe old API carries no module structure — a cell is a bare type with a\nnominated `zero` element — so this forgets structure rather than adding\nany. It exists so that a *real* spectral sequence can reach the downstream\ntheorems that were written against the old class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_two_of_bounded_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_two_of_bounded_support","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L190-L200","doc":"The legacy class, discharged from **boundedness alone** when the window is\nnarrow enough to put collapse at `E_2` — that is, `N ≤ 1`.\n\nNarrow, but not empty, and it is the first discharge of\n`GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2` in this corpus that is neither `PUnit` nor an\nassumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_of_bounded_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_of_bounded_support","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L145-L188","doc":"**Bounded support forces collapse.**\n\nIf every page vanishes outside the filtration window `0 ≤ p ≤ N`, the\nspectral sequence collapses at `N + 1`.\n\nThe argument is the standard one and it uses no property of the filtration\nbeyond its width. `d_r` shifts `p` by `r`, so once `r > N` the differential\nout of any surviving cell lands at `p + r > N`, outside the window, where\nthe target is zero. Cells already outside the window have zero *source*.\nEither way the map is zero.\n\n**This is the theorem the corpus's mass formula actually needs.**\n`conj:phi-q-categorical-truncation` states that the brane-tower sum\ntruncates at `k⋆`, the maximum GB-depth among the support partitions, and\nthat \"truncation at any deeper level yields the identical categorical\nvalue\" — a boundedness claim. Boundedness is weaker than\n`S-GB-spectral-collapse` and, as this shows, it is *provable* rather than\nassumed.\n\nWhat it does **not** give is collapse at `E_2` specifically: it yields\ncollapse at `N + 1`, where `N` is the window width. The mass formula needs\n`k⋆` to be the max GB-depth rather than something larger, so the strong\nform is still an assertion. Do not read this as discharging it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.page_stabilises_of_anticommuting_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.page_stabilises_of_anticommuting_involution","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L131-L141","doc":"**The payoff**: such a spectral sequence stabilises from `r₀` on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_of_anticommuting_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.collapses_of_anticommuting_involution","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L111-L129","doc":"**Collapse from an anticommuting involution.**\n\nA `PagedSS` whose pages carry involutions, whose differentials anticommute\nwith them, and whose pages from `r₀` on are pointwise fixed, collapses at\n`r₀`.\n\nThe \"pointwise fixed\" hypothesis is what remains to be verified for the\nGröbner filtration; it is stated as a hypothesis rather than assumed,\nwhich is the whole difference between this and `GBFiltrationCollapsesAtE2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.eq_zero_of_anticommuting_involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.eq_zero_of_anticommuting_involution","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L89-L109","doc":"**The vanishing criterion.**\n\nA differential that anticommutes with an involution, from a purely\nself-dual page to a purely self-dual page, is zero.\n\nNo sleight of hand: with both sides fixed the two facts are `d x = ⋆(d x)`\nand `⋆(d x) = −d x`, so `d x = −d x` and 2-torsion-freeness finishes. The\nhonest description is that anticommutation supplies the *second* of the two\nparity facts `BarGradedCollapse.map_eq_zero_of_parity_mismatch` demands as\na hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.isAntiSelfDual_image_of_selfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SpectralCollapseCriteria.isAntiSelfDual_image_of_selfDual","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SpectralCollapseCriteria.lean#L75-L87","doc":"**Anticommutation turns evenness of the source into oddness of the image.**\n\nThis is the reusable content of the file: `⋆(d x) = −d(⋆x)`, so if `x` is\nfixed by the source involution then `d x` is negated by the target's. One\npage-wide parity hypothesis is thereby replaced by a check on the map. ","signatureChunk":0}]}